2. WHAT YOU MAY DO (no fee, no permission needed)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Subject to the conditions below, any person is granted a personal,
non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

  (a) USE — install and run Outlaw OS on as many of your own machines as you
      like, for personal, educational, or internal purposes.
  (b) STUDY — read, compile, and inspect the source code.
  (c) MODIFY LOCALLY — change the Work on your own machines for your own use,
      and for the purpose of developing improvements to submit back (Section 3).
  (d) TEST — download, run, and evaluate pre-release / beta builds, and report
      results (including the in-OS stability reviewer).
  (e) SUGGEST CHANGES — submit bug reports, feature requests, and patches /
      pull requests to the Author's official repository.

